// The first walk down the gangway into Portvolt. Later visits answer with
// the slot entries in lore/east/portvolt.lute; on Wednesdays the market
// (east.portvoltMarket) plays after whichever greeting wins.

## The harbor

::bg{location="portvolt-harbor" time="day"}
::music{action="change" mood="upbeat" volume="normal"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: Portvolt. Cranes, gulls, a lighthouse on the point, and every roof strung with wires that hum in the salt wind.
::auto{character="portvoltHarbormaster" anchor="left" action="enter"}
@portvoltHarbormaster{code="0010"}: Off the Meridian? Welcome to Portvolt. Monster Center's up the hill, Mart beside it, and Lt. Volta's gym is past the thin tree on the east road.
@portvoltHarbormaster{code="0020"}: The tree's the council's business. They've been "about to cut it" for a year. You'd need a monster that knows Cut, and a badge to say you're allowed.
::auto{character="portvoltHarbormaster" action="exit"}

## The east road

@narrator{code="0020"}: Halfway up the east road, a boy with spiky hair is kicking the thin tree.
::auto{character="rival" anchor="right" action="enter"}
@rival{code="0010" emotion="angry"}: This tree is in my way. Trees shouldn't be allowed to be in people's way.
@rival{code="0020" emotion="smug"}: Doesn't matter. I heard the Bloom Gym leader is a pushover. I'll take the tunnel north and come back for the Lieutenant with two badges. You'll still be staring at this tree.
::auto{character="rival" action="exit"}
@narrator{code="0030" when="holds('canPass', ['portvoltTree'])"}: You could cut it right now. Kai didn't wait to find that out.
